00:21:12,880 --> 00:21:14,880
 Remember I said you don't have to start from scratch.

187
00:21:14,880 --> 00:21:18,880
 The stuff is now emerged and is available to you and it's free in other cases.

188
00:21:18,880 --> 00:21:21,880
 There is threat mitigation guidance.

189
00:21:21,880 --> 00:21:26,880
 So not only do you have a standard, you have things that can happen to go wrong and what you're going to do about it.

190
00:21:26,880 --> 00:21:30,880
 So a lot of your risk management is kind of ready to go for you.

191
00:21:30,880 --> 00:21:35,880
 There's responsible AI, the ethics and codes of conduct.

192
00:21:35,880 --> 00:21:37,880
 This varies by organisation.

193
00:21:37,880 --> 00:21:48,880
 AWS adopts the one that's from the OECD group, which is basically what the EU AI Act is based on as well.

194
00:21:48,880 --> 00:21:59,880
 Things like illegal workloads, for example, unless you happen to be a government agency such as mass surveillance, things like that.

195
00:21:59,880 --> 00:22:03,880
 Various ethics and codes of conduct are around about those sorts of things.

196
00:22:03,880 --> 00:22:08,880
 And generative AI specific threat mitigation and security frameworks.

197
00:22:08,880 --> 00:22:14,880
 So we have the OWASP LLM cyber security and OWASP top 10 for LLM.

198
00:22:14,880 --> 00:22:24,880
 These basically give you instant frameworks that you can use to help assess your applications and the processes by which you manage AI governance in your organisation, whatever it be.

199
00:22:24,880 --> 00:22:29,880
 EU AI Act.

200
00:22:29,880 --> 00:22:35,880
 I only bring this up because it's our favourite piece of AI regulation.

201
00:22:35,880 --> 00:22:37,880
 And it's a bit of a moving target.

202
00:22:37,880 --> 00:22:45,880
 August 2nd, just being, was supposed to be the deadline for high risk applications to be fully enforced.

203
00:22:45,880 --> 00:22:46,880
 This varies.

204
00:22:46,880 --> 00:22:58,880
 So there are still fairly significant requirements on transparency, documentation, other things like that, that need to be put in place now.

205
00:22:58,880 --> 00:23:00,880
 But there is a bit of a hiatus on high risk.

206
00:23:00,880 --> 00:23:12,880
 And high risk is anything that, for example, if I was building an application that was going to help the local Cardiff City Council allocate social housing to people who may have a disability.

207
00:23:12,880 --> 00:23:20,880
 If that was the case, then that is an example of an application that has direct legal impact on somebody's life.

208
00:23:20,880 --> 00:23:22,880
 Therefore it is high risk.

209
00:23:22,880 --> 00:23:24,880
 That's an example.

210
00:23:24,880 --> 00:23:37,880
 And illegal ones are anyone that's using, well, basically processing gender information, trade union membership, any particular characteristic under GDPR, or biometric information as well.

211
00:23:37,880 --> 00:23:38,880
 So, be careful.

212
00:23:38,880 --> 00:23:39,880
 Right.

