217
00:23:54,880 --> 00:24:06,880
 What we're seeing happening with our FSI customers is that they are making this sort of three tier, or three lines of defence, when it comes to the organisational controls around AI management.

218
00:24:06,880 --> 00:24:08,880
 So, tier one, own the risk.

219
00:24:08,880 --> 00:24:11,880
 Ownership, ownership, and ownership are fully important here.

220
00:24:11,880 --> 00:24:24,880
 Again, working at that large bank that cannot be named, but it's too big to fail, we had loads of systems in our data centres that were unowned and could not be shipped to another data centre because no one knew what they were and could turn them off.

221
00:24:24,880 --> 00:24:30,880
 That doesn't happen in the cloud anymore because everyone's paying for everything, and you can't hide it.

222
00:24:30,880 --> 00:24:33,880
 So, ownership is enforced.

223
00:24:33,880 --> 00:24:36,880
 Overseer risk, teams that monitor and challenge.

224
00:24:36,880 --> 00:24:40,880
 So, the first one is like builders, data scientists, maybe people like yourselves.

225
00:24:40,880 --> 00:24:43,880
 Teams that monitor and challenge, GRC, risk management.

226
00:24:43,880 --> 00:24:49,880
 There's other teams I told you that if you want your project to go live, you cannot afford to piss these people off.

227
00:24:49,880 --> 00:24:50,880
 Alright?

228
00:24:50,880 --> 00:24:52,880
 They will make you dead in the water.

229
00:24:52,880 --> 00:24:55,880
 And if that doesn't work, then the regulator will.

230
00:24:55,880 --> 00:24:56,880
 And then finally, assure the risks.

231
00:24:56,880 --> 00:24:58,880
 So, it depends on assurance.

232
00:24:58,880 --> 00:25:06,880
 The big four audit companies, whoever it may be, NCC for CREST-based pen testing, who actually test their environment and do an external report that says,

233
00:25:06,880 --> 00:25:12,880
 "I, the trusted individual organisation, did a report and I confirm that these people know what they're doing."

234
00:25:12,880 --> 00:25:22,880
 So, these are the kind of things that, you know, you need to think about putting these things in place and thinking about these governance controls.

235
00:25:22,880 --> 00:25:25,880
 It's not just about like, "Oh, I'm going to put a guardrail in."

236
00:25:25,880 --> 00:25:27,880
 You know, it's a technical control.

237
00:25:27,880 --> 00:25:30,880
 It's not an organisational or a contractual control.

238
00:25:30,880 --> 00:25:34,880
 And they are all required for AI governance to work properly.

